# Cache rules.
#
# The bug this prevents: index.html names the bundle by content hash. If a
# browser caches the HTML and we then deploy, the old hash no longer exists,
# the SPA fallback answers with index.html instead, and the page dies on
# "Unexpected token '<'" — a white screen with no explanation, in Aleppo,
# on the one machine we cannot debug.
#
# Cloudflare already serves HTML as max-age=0, must-revalidate, which is
# exactly right — so the HTML needs no rule here. Only the hashed assets do,
# and for them the hash IS the version, which is what makes "forever" safe.
#
# Do NOT add a broad /admin/* rule: every matching rule is applied, so it
# would stamp no-cache onto these files as well and undo the whole point.

/admin/_expo/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/admin/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
